1
00:02:31,067 --> 00:02:40,667
All pirates searching for the treasure One Piece must brave the second half of the Grand Line.

2
00:02:41,147 --> 00:02:44,947
These wild and dangerous seas are known as the New World.

3
00:02:46,327 --> 00:02:51,607
Gold Roger and his crew were the only men to ever chart these waters and learn all the secrets they held.

4
00:02:52,067 --> 00:02:58,167
For the rest of the pirates of the world, this has proven to be the end of the road, a graveyard of dreams.

5
00:02:58,167 --> 00:03:08,527
Now, Monkey D. Luffy, a boy whose body became rubber after eating the gum gum fruit, set sail into the New World with his faithful crew.

6
00:03:09,067 --> 00:03:12,027
I'm going to be the king of the pirates!

7
00:03:15,687 --> 00:03:23,787
During their journey to the New World, Luffy and his crew arrive on Fishman Island, which is located 10,000 meters below sea level.

8
00:03:23,787 --> 00:03:31,247
The Fishman Pirates, led by Hordy Jones and assisted by Vander Decken, plot to overthrow King Neptune.

9
00:03:33,027 --> 00:03:36,687
It's not long before the Straw Hats get pulled into the conflict.

10
00:03:38,187 --> 00:03:45,727
Thankfully, two individuals rose up on Fishman Island, individuals who had helped change the course of our beleaguered history.

11
00:03:45,727 --> 00:03:50,067
The first was Queen Otohime.

12
00:03:51,067 --> 00:03:57,187
Then there was him, the legendary hero named Fisher Tiger, who freed countless slaves.

13
00:03:58,627 --> 00:04:05,567
Nevertheless, they fought for our future, and both of their tales end in tragedy.

14
00:04:07,967 --> 00:04:11,867
A hero who freed the slaves, an adventurer tiger!

15
00:04:11,867 --> 00:04:23,707
I'm going to tell you an important story from our past.

16
00:04:24,167 --> 00:04:29,767
Regretfully, the incidents within this tale set in motion Arlong's rampage in the East Blue.

17
00:04:30,627 --> 00:04:33,367
I hope this can bring us to some understanding.

18
00:04:35,427 --> 00:04:36,707
Yeah, I'm listening.

19
00:04:36,707 --> 00:04:36,767
I'm listening.

20
00:04:41,867 --> 00:04:51,567
Before I get into the details, you must know how our world was 16 years ago.

21
00:04:58,327 --> 00:04:59,207
Move it!

22
00:05:00,427 --> 00:05:01,027
Please!

23
00:05:01,967 --> 00:05:02,727
Stop him!

24
00:05:02,927 --> 00:05:04,407
He's getting away with our money!

25
00:05:05,227 --> 00:05:06,647
Somebody do something!

26
00:05:06,647 --> 00:05:12,587
Just stay out of my way, got it?

27
00:05:12,727 --> 00:05:16,047
Because you don't want to see what I'll do to this girl if you try to be a hero.

28
00:05:19,507 --> 00:05:20,027
Huh?

29
00:05:20,487 --> 00:05:21,347
Your Majesty?

30
00:05:24,067 --> 00:05:25,547
Wait, don't go that way!

31
00:05:26,007 --> 00:05:28,447
You shouldn't involve yourself with such a thing!

32
00:05:28,787 --> 00:05:30,627
This is not our responsibility!

33
00:05:32,087 --> 00:05:33,047
Please, wait!

34
00:05:33,227 --> 00:05:33,987
Queen Otohime!

35
00:05:33,987 --> 00:05:37,427
Who's that?

36
00:05:37,847 --> 00:05:38,907
Don't come any closer!

37
00:05:39,087 --> 00:05:39,767
I'll shoot!

38
00:05:42,907 --> 00:05:44,767
I warned you!

39
00:05:54,767 --> 00:05:55,767
I missed?

40
00:05:56,187 --> 00:05:56,707
Dammit!

41
00:05:57,007 --> 00:05:57,807
Get back!

42
00:05:57,807 --> 00:05:57,867
I missed!

43
00:05:57,867 --> 00:05:58,727
Damn it!

44
00:05:58,727 --> 00:05:59,727
Get back!

45
00:05:59,727 --> 00:05:59,867
I missed!

46
00:05:59,867 --> 00:06:00,867
Damn it!

47
00:06:00,867 --> 00:06:01,867
Get back!

48
00:06:01,867 --> 00:06:02,867
I missed!

49
00:06:02,867 --> 00:06:03,867
I missed!

50
00:06:03,867 --> 00:06:04,947
I missed you!

51
00:06:04,947 --> 00:06:08,187
I got you!

52
00:06:24,187 --> 00:06:27,227
Wait, isn't that Queen Otohime?

53
00:06:30,067 --> 00:06:31,627
My hair!

54
00:06:31,647 --> 00:06:32,547
Hurry, Doctor!

55
00:06:32,547 --> 00:06:34,927
Your Highness, let me take a look.

56
00:06:37,627 --> 00:06:39,207
It's fractured, I'm afraid.

57
00:06:39,647 --> 00:06:41,507
She hit him once and broke her hand?

58
00:06:41,887 --> 00:06:42,627
It's fine.

59
00:06:44,787 --> 00:06:45,967
Queen Otohime!

60
00:06:48,687 --> 00:06:49,847
The Queen?

61
00:06:50,587 --> 00:06:54,747
Why would you do something as foolish and selfish as robbing your fellow people?

62
00:06:54,987 --> 00:06:58,427
What do you care? Like a rich member of the royal family could understand.

63
00:06:58,427 --> 00:07:02,687
I got ten kids waiting at home, and all they do is cry, cause they're hungry!

64
00:07:03,887 --> 00:07:05,227
All the more reason!

65
00:07:09,627 --> 00:07:11,007
No! Queen Otohime!

66
00:07:11,387 --> 00:07:13,147
You must stop hitting him, please!

67
00:07:13,487 --> 00:07:16,547
They're much too delicate, you will only make your injury worse!

68
00:07:16,547 --> 00:07:19,287
I don't care! I have to do this!

69
00:07:19,907 --> 00:07:23,527
Even if my hand must shatter to pieces, he will learn his lesson!

70
00:07:28,207 --> 00:07:31,167
Do you think your children would be happy if they knew the truth?

71
00:07:31,507 --> 00:07:33,447
If they knew their father was a thief?

72
00:07:33,447 --> 00:07:40,347
You should be trying to live your life in a way that makes them proud!

73
00:07:49,027 --> 00:07:49,667
However,

74
00:07:50,527 --> 00:07:52,827
I owe you

75
00:07:52,827 --> 00:07:55,827
an apology.

76
00:07:55,827 --> 00:08:00,947
Please forgive me!

77
00:08:02,947 --> 00:08:04,467
Even though I'm your queen,

78
00:08:04,987 --> 00:08:10,267
I've been completely ignorant to the hardships that one of my subjects has been forced to endure.

79
00:08:11,567 --> 00:08:13,307
My heart can't take it.

80
00:08:14,067 --> 00:08:15,847
Your worries and your pain,

81
00:08:16,087 --> 00:08:17,527
they're killing me!

82
00:08:17,527 --> 00:08:24,087
You must have had a reason for doing this!

83
00:08:24,647 --> 00:08:26,267
I don't know.

84
00:08:26,827 --> 00:08:28,267
It's not that I wanted to.

85
00:08:29,047 --> 00:08:29,647
But I,

86
00:08:29,767 --> 00:08:31,927
I felt like there was no other way.

87
00:08:32,787 --> 00:08:34,847
Somebody sent fire to my store

88
00:08:34,847 --> 00:08:36,707
and stole all my money.

89
00:08:37,187 --> 00:08:38,467
We couldn't save anything

90
00:08:38,467 --> 00:08:39,687
before we burned down.

91
00:08:40,027 --> 00:08:40,947
Just like that,

92
00:08:41,007 --> 00:08:42,247
I didn't have a job.

93
00:08:42,807 --> 00:08:44,207
My debt started piling up,

94
00:08:44,607 --> 00:08:45,967
and now my kids are starving.

95
00:08:45,967 --> 00:08:49,067
I'm sorry that happened.

96
00:08:49,567 --> 00:08:50,787
And I understand.

97
00:08:51,187 --> 00:08:52,327
I really do,

98
00:08:52,467 --> 00:08:53,287
but...

99
00:08:53,287 --> 00:08:54,007
It's wrong!

100
00:08:55,067 --> 00:08:57,267
If you do to others what was done to you,

101
00:08:57,447 --> 00:08:58,827
the cycle will never end!

102
00:08:58,907 --> 00:08:59,667
I'm sorry!

103
00:09:00,607 --> 00:09:01,987
No, I'm sorry!

104
00:09:02,527 --> 00:09:04,687
We weren't there for you in your time of need,

105
00:09:04,747 --> 00:09:06,867
so that makes us accountable as well.

106
00:09:07,187 --> 00:09:07,747
Your Highness,

107
00:09:07,927 --> 00:09:09,467
it's really not your fault.

108
00:09:09,767 --> 00:09:12,347
But that's a terribly generous thing for you to say.

109
00:09:12,387 --> 00:09:13,687
It's still wrong, though!

110
00:09:14,007 --> 00:09:14,587
I know!

111
00:09:14,807 --> 00:09:15,387
I know!

112
00:09:15,387 --> 00:09:16,847
Then don't do it!

113
00:09:17,567 --> 00:09:18,827
You've changed me!

114
00:09:18,947 --> 00:09:19,927
And my whole life!

115
00:09:20,167 --> 00:09:21,367
Thank you so much!

116
00:09:21,547 --> 00:09:23,347
After seeing how much you cried for me,

117
00:09:23,647 --> 00:09:25,467
I'll never steal again!

118
00:09:25,527 --> 00:09:26,567
I know that you won't!

119
00:09:26,927 --> 00:09:28,267
Best of luck in the future!

120
00:09:28,807 --> 00:09:31,227
We're so lucky to have a member of the royal family

121
00:09:31,227 --> 00:09:32,887
who's not afraid to share the troubles

122
00:09:32,887 --> 00:09:34,547
of common people like us.

123
00:09:34,767 --> 00:09:36,607
She nearly had me crying along with her,

124
00:09:36,727 --> 00:09:39,127
though I certainly hope she doesn't break her hand next time.

125
00:09:39,367 --> 00:09:42,307
Our Queen Otohime is a one-of-a-kind ruler,

126
00:09:42,307 --> 00:09:43,447
or I can tell you that much!

127
00:09:43,767 --> 00:09:45,187
She has such a kind heart.

128
00:09:45,607 --> 00:09:46,427
And look there!

129
00:09:46,807 --> 00:09:48,807
Even the children of the kingdom adore her!

130
00:09:48,907 --> 00:09:49,967
Queen Otohime!

131
00:09:52,067 --> 00:09:55,027
I'll do everything I can to protect your smiling faces!

132
00:09:55,027 --> 00:09:59,467
You're nose is running terribly!

133
00:09:59,467 --> 00:10:01,927
If I don't reprimand you for it, who will?

134
00:10:02,727 --> 00:10:06,147
You look ridiculous with mucus dribbling out of just one side.

135
00:10:06,567 --> 00:10:08,907
It's more dignified to dribble from both nostrils.

136
00:10:08,907 --> 00:10:14,727
Such a tender moment!

137
00:10:15,567 --> 00:10:16,487
I guess so.

138
00:10:17,327 --> 00:10:19,787
No one was more passionate or loving.

139
00:10:20,627 --> 00:10:24,767
Every day Queen Otohime descended from the palace to address the nation.

140
00:10:25,447 --> 00:10:26,867
That day was no different.

141
00:10:27,867 --> 00:10:31,407
The time has come for us to relocate the Ryugu kingdom to the surface.

142
00:10:32,047 --> 00:10:33,427
Our skins are different colors,

143
00:10:33,807 --> 00:10:35,347
and we do not look the same.

144
00:10:35,347 --> 00:10:39,427
These are the things the humans say in order to avoid understanding us

145
00:10:39,427 --> 00:10:40,907
and our unique way of life.

146
00:10:41,087 --> 00:10:42,487
But that's why we should move.

147
00:10:42,847 --> 00:10:44,207
To understand each other.

148
00:10:45,127 --> 00:10:47,547
Our worlds are 10,000 meters apart.

149
00:10:47,907 --> 00:10:51,207
So, that is also the distance between our ways of thinking.

150
00:10:55,427 --> 00:10:56,907
I know you're afraid.

151
00:10:57,587 --> 00:11:01,407
After all, the humans who come to our island are pirates and criminals.

152
00:11:01,407 --> 00:11:05,447
And the humans who buy our people from kidnappers like them

153
00:11:05,447 --> 00:11:07,247
are cruel and corrupt nobles.

154
00:11:08,227 --> 00:11:11,307
It's true that our only exposure to humans has been negative,

155
00:11:11,827 --> 00:11:14,867
but that doesn't mean we can judge all humans the same.

156
00:11:15,407 --> 00:11:18,627
I believe in my heart that there are good ones among them as well.

157
00:11:19,287 --> 00:11:21,067
And thus, to improve relations,

158
00:11:21,287 --> 00:11:23,887
we must move our kingdom to be under the same sun.

159
00:11:23,887 --> 00:11:28,987
It is my goal to express our intention

160
00:11:28,987 --> 00:11:32,247
to relocate above sea level at this year's world summit.

161
00:11:32,447 --> 00:11:35,167
But in order to do that, I need all of you to sign.

162
00:11:38,747 --> 00:11:43,227
While, uh, I admit it sounds like a good idea in theory, but...

163
00:11:43,227 --> 00:11:46,187
Just the thought of living near humans is...

164
00:11:46,187 --> 00:11:46,887
Well...

165
00:11:46,887 --> 00:11:52,387
I understand how you feel.

166
00:11:52,807 --> 00:11:55,147
However, this is our chance to make a real change

167
00:11:55,147 --> 00:11:56,907
rather than suffering in silence.

168
00:11:58,867 --> 00:11:59,467
Please!

169
00:12:01,347 --> 00:12:03,147
Look, I'm sorry, but...

170
00:12:03,147 --> 00:12:03,347
No.

171
00:12:03,347 --> 00:12:14,467
It's no use.

172
00:12:15,387 --> 00:12:17,507
History can't be fought so easily.

173
00:12:26,547 --> 00:12:27,687
Hello, everyone!

174
00:12:27,947 --> 00:12:28,727
I'm home!

175
00:12:28,727 --> 00:12:29,187
Ah!

176
00:12:29,187 --> 00:12:37,447
I'm home!

177
00:12:37,807 --> 00:12:38,487
Shirahoshi!

178
00:12:45,107 --> 00:12:51,347
I hope you can forgive me, darling.

179
00:12:52,027 --> 00:12:53,667
Mommy didn't mean to be so late.

180
00:12:53,667 --> 00:12:59,867
Even with your nose running on one side,

181
00:12:59,967 --> 00:13:01,067
you're still beautiful.

182
00:13:01,767 --> 00:13:04,027
We stayed with her the entire time you were gone

183
00:13:04,027 --> 00:13:05,287
so she'd feel safe, Mother.

184
00:13:05,507 --> 00:13:06,447
It's true, Mother!

185
00:13:06,547 --> 00:13:07,327
We did!

186
00:13:07,447 --> 00:13:08,947
I have such brave sons.

187
00:13:09,587 --> 00:13:11,127
But what happened to your hand?

188
00:13:11,267 --> 00:13:12,367
Are you okay?

189
00:13:12,887 --> 00:13:14,027
Oh, don't worry, dear.

190
00:13:14,087 --> 00:13:14,667
It's nothing.

191
00:13:15,327 --> 00:13:15,587
See?

192
00:13:16,387 --> 00:13:18,607
To ensure you all have a bright future,

193
00:13:19,047 --> 00:13:19,827
I would suffer.

194
00:13:20,827 --> 00:13:22,487
So much worse than this.

195
00:13:22,487 --> 00:13:27,467
If Queen Otohime wants to make announcements,

196
00:13:27,747 --> 00:13:29,327
she really should do them by video

197
00:13:29,327 --> 00:13:31,207
rather than going down there in person.

198
00:13:31,707 --> 00:13:34,747
Unfortunately, thanks to her strong observation, Haki,

199
00:13:35,247 --> 00:13:37,747
doing something like that would go against her very nature.

200
00:13:38,347 --> 00:13:40,947
She would rather win the hearts of the citizens in person

201
00:13:40,947 --> 00:13:41,967
than from the palace.

202
00:13:42,707 --> 00:13:45,207
It's one of Otohime's guiding principles.

203
00:13:45,747 --> 00:13:47,167
Not even I can change that.

204
00:13:47,167 --> 00:13:49,707
She's constantly putting her life at risk

205
00:13:49,707 --> 00:13:52,427
with all those human pirates coming and going on the island.

206
00:13:52,427 --> 00:13:55,067
We know you're on good terms with Whitebeard,

207
00:13:55,267 --> 00:13:58,507
and to some extent his influence can protect her while she's there.

208
00:13:58,967 --> 00:14:00,707
But anything could happen.

209
00:14:01,147 --> 00:14:03,767
That is a fact of which she is all too aware.

210
00:14:04,307 --> 00:14:06,507
And yet, it does nothing to deter her.

211
00:14:06,847 --> 00:14:08,967
For the world Otohime dreams of

212
00:14:08,967 --> 00:14:12,107
is far more than a simple fantasy.

213
00:14:13,547 --> 00:14:18,087
After all, unifying our peoples was also the ambition of our ancestors,

214
00:14:18,707 --> 00:14:21,887
although they were never able to make that vision a reality.

215
00:14:22,687 --> 00:14:23,107
What?

216
00:14:23,347 --> 00:14:25,567
I'm afraid that I don't follow your majesty.

217
00:14:25,567 --> 00:14:30,247
I can't stop Otohime from doing what she thinks is right.

218
00:14:30,867 --> 00:14:33,147
So it's up to you to keep her safe.

219
00:14:33,567 --> 00:14:34,227
Yes, sir.

220
00:14:39,487 --> 00:14:41,787
Hey, where you going, fish girl?

221
00:14:41,987 --> 00:14:42,327
Sir?

222
00:14:42,587 --> 00:14:44,367
How about some special service?

223
00:14:44,907 --> 00:14:45,567
I'm sorry.

224
00:14:45,867 --> 00:14:47,287
I don't think I know what you mean.

225
00:14:47,987 --> 00:14:48,427
Huh?

226
00:14:48,847 --> 00:14:51,087
Come on now, don't be such a snob.

227
00:14:51,367 --> 00:14:53,387
We know how you fish men are.

228
00:14:55,567 --> 00:15:02,367
What's wrong?

229
00:15:02,807 --> 00:15:04,607
You punks got something to say?

230
00:15:08,527 --> 00:15:10,067
Get out of here.

231
00:15:15,707 --> 00:15:17,787
You're ruining my meal.

232
00:15:19,867 --> 00:15:20,907
Sorry.

233
00:15:25,567 --> 00:15:49,007
This Queen Otohime certainly seemed unique, if nothing else.

234
00:15:49,007 --> 00:15:51,507
Sounds like she was a crybaby, too.

235
00:15:51,627 --> 00:15:52,907
Did you inherit that from her?

236
00:15:53,127 --> 00:15:54,567
Um, yes.

237
00:15:54,747 --> 00:15:55,987
I suppose I did.

238
00:15:56,327 --> 00:15:56,947
Hold on.

239
00:15:57,007 --> 00:15:58,847
You used to be a soldier for the kingdom?

240
00:15:59,627 --> 00:16:01,947
When you grow up in the fish man district,

241
00:16:02,087 --> 00:16:03,507
where you know nothing but fighting,

242
00:16:03,667 --> 00:16:06,727
there aren't a lot of career path options available to you.

243
00:16:07,067 --> 00:16:08,227
You don't say.

244
00:16:08,587 --> 00:16:09,367
That's rough.

245
00:16:09,927 --> 00:16:11,367
Is that where you're from, Hachi?

246
00:16:11,367 --> 00:16:13,687
It sounds like a pretty bad neighborhood.

247
00:16:15,007 --> 00:16:16,127
It was.

248
00:16:17,107 --> 00:16:18,027
Believe me.

249
00:16:19,087 --> 00:16:22,467
Originally, it was an orphanage for children with no living relatives.

250
00:16:23,567 --> 00:16:28,067
But in time, the orphanage became too much for the administrators to handle.

251
00:16:28,887 --> 00:16:34,067
Before long, it became a lawless area that caught the eye of delinquents from all over the island.

252
00:16:34,067 --> 00:16:39,227
Back then, Fisher Tiger was the closest thing we had to a leader,

253
00:16:39,627 --> 00:16:41,367
but he left to have his own adventures.

254
00:16:42,687 --> 00:16:46,707
I'd been his second in command, but I went on to join Neptune's army.

255
00:16:48,047 --> 00:16:49,587
And despite being fish men,

256
00:16:50,127 --> 00:16:52,447
Macro and some others started helping the kidnappers.

257
00:16:53,407 --> 00:16:54,867
As for everyone else,

258
00:16:55,527 --> 00:16:58,807
they all left, following their own pursuits.

259
00:16:59,707 --> 00:17:02,067
Until one day...

260
00:17:02,067 --> 00:17:04,647
Please, give them back!

261
00:17:04,927 --> 00:17:06,947
Oh, you almost had them that time.

262
00:17:07,067 --> 00:17:08,167
Hey, knock it off!

263
00:17:08,307 --> 00:17:10,867
Do you realize how hard it was for her to get all those signatures?

264
00:17:11,187 --> 00:17:13,687
Yeah, and you realize I don't care, right?

265
00:17:17,287 --> 00:17:20,047
These papers aren't gonna change a damn thing!

266
00:17:20,347 --> 00:17:20,767
Get it?

267
00:17:21,127 --> 00:17:22,407
Hey, cut it out!

268
00:17:22,707 --> 00:17:24,327
You fish men district reject!

269
00:17:24,847 --> 00:17:25,147
Huh?

270
00:17:27,187 --> 00:17:30,327
You think you're better than me because of where I'm from?

271
00:17:32,067 --> 00:17:33,527
Let go of me!

272
00:17:33,907 --> 00:17:35,847
You got it backwards, pal.

273
00:17:36,567 --> 00:17:39,187
I'm the captain of the Arlong Pirates,

274
00:17:39,387 --> 00:17:41,427
and you're just a nobody.

275
00:17:41,947 --> 00:17:45,007
I clean up all the human garbage you let run wild.

276
00:17:45,347 --> 00:17:48,387
Pirates so pathetic, they can't even breathe in the water.

277
00:17:48,707 --> 00:17:51,927
You guys in Neptune's army should be thanking us.

278
00:17:52,267 --> 00:17:54,567
Maybe I should beat a donation out of you.

279
00:17:55,007 --> 00:17:56,667
Please, I'm in trouble over here.

280
00:17:56,867 --> 00:17:58,427
He's gonna kill me, Boss Jinbei.

281
00:17:58,927 --> 00:17:59,407
Jinbei.

282
00:17:59,407 --> 00:18:02,987
All right, punk.

283
00:18:03,487 --> 00:18:05,627
Just put the rookie down and walk away.

284
00:18:05,947 --> 00:18:07,887
He's weak, but he's one of my men.

285
00:18:08,507 --> 00:18:10,307
And as for those papers you've taken,

286
00:18:10,887 --> 00:18:12,647
they may not mean anything to us,

287
00:18:12,687 --> 00:18:14,667
but they're quite important to her majesty.

288
00:18:15,207 --> 00:18:15,807
Give them back.

289
00:18:15,827 --> 00:18:17,887
That's Boss Jinbei of Neptune's army!

290
00:18:18,047 --> 00:18:19,027
It'll help us!

291
00:18:19,247 --> 00:18:19,647
Yeah!

292
00:18:19,647 --> 00:18:21,587
They call you Boss!

293
00:18:21,827 --> 00:18:23,547
How'd you get that kind of respect?

294
00:18:24,027 --> 00:18:27,227
Sounds more like the title of a gang leader than a soldier, though.

295
00:18:27,467 --> 00:18:29,487
I told you to let him go, Arlong.

296
00:18:30,927 --> 00:18:32,187
All right, fine.

297
00:18:34,307 --> 00:18:34,827
Here.

298
00:18:34,827 --> 00:18:38,147
So are we all good now, brother?

299
00:18:38,407 --> 00:18:38,807
Huh?

300
00:18:39,047 --> 00:18:39,527
Brother?

301
00:18:40,227 --> 00:18:41,207
It's been a while.

302
00:18:41,567 --> 00:18:44,627
But I can always tell when someone's from the Fistman district.

303
00:18:45,127 --> 00:18:46,687
Don't lump me in with you.

304
00:18:47,087 --> 00:18:49,107
You went off and became a lousy pirate.

305
00:18:49,627 --> 00:18:50,387
You're scum.

306
00:18:50,767 --> 00:18:51,127
Hmph.

307
00:18:51,607 --> 00:18:52,927
Don't call me that, brother.

308
00:18:53,447 --> 00:18:54,807
Then how about trash?

309
00:18:54,887 --> 00:18:55,727
Oh, that's it!

310
00:18:56,087 --> 00:18:57,327
Doesn't matter where we're from.

311
00:18:57,387 --> 00:18:58,547
You can't talk to me like that!

312
00:18:58,547 --> 00:18:58,847
Hey!

313
00:18:59,247 --> 00:19:00,087
Hey, everyone!

314
00:19:00,647 --> 00:19:02,187
Fisher Tiger's come home!

315
00:19:02,627 --> 00:19:03,607
I don't believe it!

316
00:19:03,827 --> 00:19:04,647
Tiger's back!

317
00:19:05,167 --> 00:19:06,087
He's here!

318
00:19:06,287 --> 00:19:07,147
How is the trip?

319
00:19:07,627 --> 00:19:08,767
It's brother time!

320
00:19:08,847 --> 00:19:10,007
Finally made it back!

321
00:19:10,187 --> 00:19:10,907
Hi, Jinbei.

322
00:19:11,387 --> 00:19:12,067
And Arlong.

323
00:19:12,367 --> 00:19:14,467
It sure looks like you two have been doing well.

324
00:19:14,687 --> 00:19:16,947
That was quite a lengthy voyage you took.

325
00:19:17,387 --> 00:19:19,007
Yeah, an eventful one, too.

326
00:19:19,367 --> 00:19:21,287
Now that you're here, you can see my ship!

327
00:19:21,567 --> 00:19:21,947
Later.

328
00:19:21,947 --> 00:19:22,027
Later.

329
00:19:22,367 --> 00:19:24,267
First, I need to go to the Ryugu Palace.

330
00:19:24,987 --> 00:19:26,267
I can show you the way.

331
00:19:26,927 --> 00:19:28,987
He has no need for a lousy pirate.

332
00:19:29,307 --> 00:19:29,567
Huh?

333
00:19:30,087 --> 00:19:32,687
That's not how Big Brother feels about me at all!

334
00:19:32,947 --> 00:19:33,507
Heh heh heh.

335
00:19:33,907 --> 00:19:34,747
Come on, guys.

336
00:19:34,887 --> 00:19:35,527
Don't fight.

337
00:19:49,347 --> 00:19:51,787
You're telling me you're going to free the slaves?

338
00:19:52,627 --> 00:19:54,507
Surely you can't be serious.

339
00:19:55,067 --> 00:19:56,247
I'm afraid I am.

340
00:19:56,787 --> 00:19:58,127
I can't stand it anymore.

341
00:19:58,127 --> 00:20:01,827
The thought of our people living a nightmare.

342
00:20:02,687 --> 00:20:07,387
Even as we're speaking right now, our people are being treated like animals.

343
00:20:08,327 --> 00:20:09,627
Yes, but...

344
00:20:09,627 --> 00:20:10,587
My mind's made up.

345
00:20:11,247 --> 00:20:15,547
I just wanted to tell you before I did anything, since it's going to cause you a lot of trouble.

346
00:20:16,067 --> 00:20:18,707
Despite that, I ask that you keep this to yourselves.

347
00:20:20,407 --> 00:20:23,147
Tell me, why are you so adamant about this?

348
00:20:23,907 --> 00:20:25,287
What did you see on your trip?

349
00:20:25,287 --> 00:20:33,327
I saw human nature.

350
00:20:33,327 --> 00:20:37,447
I saw human nature.

351
00:20:37,447 --> 00:21:06,047
Not long after that, Tiger made his move.

352
00:21:07,447 --> 00:21:11,547
This is bad!

353
00:21:11,547 --> 00:21:12,947
What's the problem?

354
00:21:12,947 --> 00:21:14,747
Oh, good, I found you, boss.

355
00:21:14,747 --> 00:21:15,947
It's about Tiger.

356
00:21:15,947 --> 00:21:19,747
It seems he attacked the Celestial Dragons.

357
00:21:19,747 --> 00:21:21,247
No, that can't be true.

358
00:21:24,347 --> 00:21:28,847
Fisher Tiger unleashed all-out war on the Holy Land of Mariejoie.

359
00:21:28,847 --> 00:21:32,747
For freeing the slaves, he forever became a hero to our people

360
00:21:32,747 --> 00:21:34,747
and a criminal to the world government.

361
00:21:37,447 --> 00:21:43,947
Consider this my resignation from the army.

362
00:21:43,947 --> 00:21:44,947
Jinbei!

363
00:21:44,947 --> 00:21:47,947
You would walk away from your sworn duty?

364
00:21:47,947 --> 00:21:52,947
Much to my surprise, I've enjoyed my role as this island's protector.

365
00:21:52,947 --> 00:21:57,447
However, my obligation to this kingdom does not outweigh my debt of honor.

366
00:21:57,447 --> 00:22:04,947
It looks like Big Brother Tai has finally made his move.

367
00:22:04,947 --> 00:22:06,947
All right, O-Long Pirates.

368
00:22:06,947 --> 00:22:08,947
From here on, we work for Fisher Tiger.

369
00:22:08,947 --> 00:22:10,947
Let's go, men!

370
00:22:10,947 --> 00:22:18,447
Before long, every ruffian from the Fishman District had assembled to fight by his side.

371
00:22:18,447 --> 00:22:23,447
How does it feel to be lumped in with lousy pirate scum?

372
00:22:23,447 --> 00:22:24,947
Come.

373
00:22:24,947 --> 00:22:28,947
It's us against the world from now on.

374
00:22:28,947 --> 00:22:33,947
If you're truly ready for the days ahead, then step up!

375
00:22:33,947 --> 00:22:41,447
All who accepted the sun mark that day became brothers.

376
00:22:41,447 --> 00:22:44,447
It was a symbol that enveloped the brand given to slaves.

377
00:22:44,447 --> 00:22:49,447
No longer could anyone distinguish which of us had always been free

378
00:22:49,447 --> 00:22:52,447
and which of us had to fight to reclaim that freedom.

379
00:22:52,447 --> 00:23:08,947
And that's how a bunch of lowlifes from the Fishman District rose up as the Sun Pirates.

380
00:23:08,947 --> 00:23:14,947
Fisher Tiger attacks the Holy Land of Marie Joie, freeing those enslaved by the Celestial Dragons.

381
00:23:14,947 --> 00:23:21,947
As his journey continues, he encounters a human girl with a tragic past who he vows to reunite with her family.

382
00:23:21,947 --> 00:23:27,447
Unfortunately, his actions have drawn the attention of a very deadly adversary.

383
00:23:27,447 --> 00:23:32,447
On the next One Piece, Kizaru appears! A trap to catch Tiger!

384
00:23:32,447 --> 00:23:35,447
I'm gonna be king of the pirates!

